{
  "id": "fluency-l7-characteristic-equation",
  "lesson": "l7-characteristic-equation",
  "title": "Fluency: the characteristic equation",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 12,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "real-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "find two real characteristic roots",
      "vars": {
        "r1": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "r2": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["y", "x", "u"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "-(r1 + r2)",
        "c": "r1*r2"
      },
      "where": ["r1 < r2", "r1 + r2 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Find both roots of the characteristic equation of ${v}''{b:+c}{v}'{c:+c}{v} = 0$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answers": ["{r1}", "{r2}"], "unordered": true, "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "accept": "${r1}$ and ${r2}$, in either order" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "signs-flipped", "value": "{-r1}, {-r2}", "line": "Those solve $r^2{-b:+c}r{c:+c} = 0$. The roots of $(r - p)(r - q)$ are $p$ and $q$, so check the signs." },
        { "id": "not-halved", "value": "{2*r1}, {2*r2}", "line": "You did not divide by $2a = 2$ in the formula." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Try ${v} = e^{{rt}}$: the characteristic equation is $r^2{b:+c}r{c:+c} = 0$.",
        "It factorises as $(r{-r1:+})(r{-r2:+}) = 0$, so $r = {r1}$ or $r = {r2}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "complex-root",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "find a complex characteristic root",
      "vars": {
        "al": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "be": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "v": { "pick": ["y", "x", "u"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "-2*al",
        "c": "al^2 + be^2",
        "disc": "4*al^2 - 4*(al^2 + be^2)",
        "nb": "2*al",
        "b2": "2*be"
      },
      "prompt": "For ${v}''{b:+c}{v}'{c:+}{v} = 0$, enter the characteristic root with positive imaginary part.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{al}{be:+c}i", "form": "rectangular", "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "other-root", "tex": "{al}{-be:+c}i", "line": "That is the other root. The question asks for the one with positive imaginary part." },
        { "id": "minus-b-dropped", "tex": "{-al}{be:+c}i", "line": "You dropped the minus on $-b$. The real part is ${nb} \\div 2 = {al}$." },
        { "id": "not-halved", "tex": "{al}{b2:+c}i", "line": "You forgot to halve $\\sqrt{{{disc}}} = {b2}i$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The characteristic equation is $r^2{b:+c}r{c:+} = 0$, with discriminant ${disc}$.",
        "$\\sqrt{{{disc}}} = {b2}i$, so $r = \\dfrac{{{nb} \\pm {b2}i}}{{2}} = {al} \\pm {be:c}i$.",
        "The root with positive imaginary part is ${al}{be:+c}i$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fit-two-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "fit two starting values",
      "vars": {
        "r1": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "r2": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "c1": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "c2": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "-(r1 + r2)",
        "c": "r1*r2",
        "y0": "c1 + c2",
        "v0": "r1*c1 + r2*c2"
      },
      "where": ["r1 < r2", "r1 + r2 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Solve $y''{b:+c}y'{c:+c}y = 0$ for $y(t)$, with $y(0) = {y0}$ and $y'(0) = {v0}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{c1:c}e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}}{c2:+c}e^{{{mono(t; r2, 1)}}}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "constants-swapped", "tex": "{c2:c}e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}}{c1:+c}e^{{{mono(t; r2, 1)}}}", "line": "You matched the constants to the wrong roots. Check $y'(0) = {r1:c}c_1{r2:+c}c_2$.", "when": "c1 != c2" },
        { "id": "one-constant", "tex": "{y0:c}e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}}", "line": "Two starting values need two constants: $y = c_1e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}} + c_2e^{{{mono(t; r2, 1)}}}$.", "when": "y0 != 0" }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The roots of $r^2{b:+c}r{c:+c} = 0$ are ${r1}$ and ${r2}$, so $y = c_1e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}} + c_2e^{{{mono(t; r2, 1)}}}$.",
        "The starting values give $c_1 + c_2 = {y0}$ and ${r1:c}c_1{r2:+c}c_2 = {v0}$.",
        "So $c_1 = {c1}$ and $c_2 = {c2}$, and $y = {c1:c}e^{{{mono(t; r1, 1)}}}{c2:+c}e^{{{mono(t; r2, 1)}}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "repeated-root",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "fit a repeated root",
      "vars": {
        "r": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "y0": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "-2*r",
        "c": "r^2",
        "v0": "k + r*y0",
        "ry": "r*y0"
      },
      "where": ["k + r*y0 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Solve $y''{b:+c}y'{c:+c}y = 0$ for $y(t)$, with $y(0) = {y0}$ and $y'(0) = {v0}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "({poly(t; k, y0)})e^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "rc1-forgotten", "tex": "({poly(t; v0, y0)})e^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}", "line": "You set $c_2 = y'(0)$. In fact $y'(0) = {r:c}c_1 + c_2$, so $c_2 = {v0} - {ry:()} = {k}$." },
        { "id": "t-term-dropped", "tex": "{y0:c}e^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}", "line": "A repeated root needs the second solution $te^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}$ as well." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The characteristic equation is $(r{-r:+})^2 = 0$, so the root ${r}$ is repeated and $y = (c_1 + c_2t)e^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}$.",
        "$y(0) = c_1 = {y0}$, and $y'(0) = {r:c}c_1 + c_2 = {v0}$ gives $c_2 = {k}$.",
        "So $y = ({poly(t; k, y0)})e^{{{mono(t; r, 1)}}}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
